# TODO - Complete the AR9565 Linux ledger and retire local references

## Objective

Complete source migration for AR9565/QCA9565 PCI 168c:0036 revisions 1.0,
1.0.1 and 1.1, assess every local reference against that target, then delete
only the repository's local Linux reference tree. The owner explicitly
requested this eventual deletion; the current partial ledger does not meet
its preconditions. This is not permission to delete other source trees,
backups, EFI contents, SDK/KDK evidence or system files.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Every current ledger path/hash is assessed as required, supporting,
      or out of scope for AR9565, with an evidence-backed rationale.
- [ ] Every required/supporting implementation scope is complete and
      integrated in committed source; record commits, destinations and
      static review. No applicable entry remains unknown or partially ported.
- [ ] Unrelated chipsets, Linux-only glue and unnecessary subsystems are
      explicitly marked not required for this target; do not port them just
      to make the inventory appear complete. Preserve any relevant protocol
      or regulatory knowledge from shared Linux sources.
- [ ] Keep existing inline source notices and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
      No additional archive, reproducibility package, source mirror or
      provenance infrastructure is required.
- [ ] Preserve HT20/HT40 variants, RX/TX gain choices, EEPROM dictionaries,
      board/regulatory semantics and the AR9565 1.1 radio postamble.
- [ ] Retained generation/inspection tools no longer require a local linux/
      tree. Retain the completed source data without requiring new builds,
      hardware experiments; necessary offline host tests are permitted.
- [ ] Review the actual directory and ledger immediately before deletion:
      no unexpected/new reference, hash mismatch or unrecorded local change
      may be discarded. A path alias or symlink must not redirect deletion.
- [ ] Once all conditions above hold, delete only this repository's local
      linux/ tree and record the retirement commit. Keep the JSONL ledger;
      do not create a second manifest or reference archive.
- [ ] Update AGENTS/README/TODO to describe retired references accurately;
      no compilation or hardware proof is required to complete this task.

## Evidence

- Initial inventory: 419 local files, with only 16 partial implementation
  records at creation. This task is OPEN and deletion is not ready.
- Record target applicability and implementation commits in the existing
  ledger. No extra preservation deliverable is required.
- Preserve Linux and SimpleBCM attribution in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md without
  expanding that file into an inventory of unrelated projects.
